    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3452b1e_d799c1f6",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-15T17:06:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not convinced that there is value to this. If there is a code path that you are aware of that can enter here which would fail the checkIsIncremental() call, then why not just fix that code path?",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1805c93_766d5c04",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1012457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-15T18:10:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, we don\u0027t know for sure what the exact code path is. We saw a couple of instances of the sequence going back to an older value in the last year and those were painful to recover from. So, we think this change is a good safety check to have to avoid any data corruptions.",
      "parentUuid": "f3452b1e_d799c1f6",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cfe105c5_ba61ba84",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-15T18:28:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But you should be able to audit all of the methods that you modified to call store() to make sure they enforce this policy, and fix them if they don\u0027t. Because if they call this with bad data, they are buggy, and I don\u0027t believe we should be adding a check to fix buggy code instead of fixing the buggy code. Of course, that won\u0027t cover potential other places which update this refs, but neither will this change currently.",
      "parentUuid": "b1805c93_766d5c04",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8ce1052_b0a33936",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-15T20:47:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I think our primary concern is the call from `acquire()`, so it\u0027s reasonable to move the `checkIsIncremental()` call above L369 as:\n\n```\ncheckIsIncremental(next);\n```\n\nOur best guess is that the `IntBlob.parse(repo, refName, rw);` in `acquire()` is somehow returning an incorrect value, but we haven\u0027t yet found the buggy code that could do that.\n\nDepending on if we wanted to protect/limit admins, we could also do a `checkIsIncremental(value)` call after L383, but that API is only used by the SSH `sequence set` command.",
      "parentUuid": "cfe105c5_ba61ba84",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86ef0351_13d792c1",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1012457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-15T21:59:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I moved `checkIsIncremental` outside the `store` helper now. It is now done immediately for the `sequence set` cmd before acquiring the lock.",
      "parentUuid": "a8ce1052_b0a33936",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "259cbd9c_3c0c679e",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T15:20:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moving this check doesn\u0027t feel right to me for the same reasons mentioned above.",
      "parentUuid": "86ef0351_13d792c1",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50f18ad1_b2d4cda8",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T22:16:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moving the check won\u0027t necessarily prevent a bad value from being written, but it will prevent it from being *used*, which I do think is a worthwhile addition.",
      "parentUuid": "259cbd9c_3c0c679e",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3acbe7a4_1f1cb529",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T17:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if a bad value is detected, should this potentially try to recover instead of failing? i.e. Should a newer value greater than lastStoredSequence be chosen (and written)? How much greater?",
      "parentUuid": "50f18ad1_b2d4cda8",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a6465af_b310cb5c",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1012457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T19:41:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While it would be nice to have auto-recovery, at least failing is a good first step to prevent the use of a bad value. Automatically selecting a *correct* value might be difficult, as it might be hard to determine one that would be universally acceptable. I think we should consider that as a separate effort, if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "3acbe7a4_1f1cb529",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d335383f_da63629f",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T19:46:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is that failing likely does not have much value. My thought is that if this situation occurs, it could result in back-to-back failures leading to admins restarting the service. Once the service is restarted, the cached value of the last value will no longer be present, and the detection of the \"rewind\" will fail. At this point the restarted server will likely continue with the rewound value anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "6a6465af_b310cb5c",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4168f17_ced97fa4",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1012457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T18:49:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it still provides value, even when we fail. When failures occur, we now at-least alert admins instead of silently rewinding the sequence. Dealing with duplicates is painful because we not only require fixing the corruption in Gerrit but also fix external systems that reference this data.\n\nYour concern is valid, though. However, I’d expect most admins to set the sequence (using the sequence set command) to a known good value, rather than restarting the service and hoping for the best. That said, if we were to choose a new value, something like `lastStoredSequence + batchSize * 1000` might be reasonable.\n\nChoosing a new value without knowing how far ahead the sequence is can be difficult, so I believe it\u0027s best to delegate this decision to the admins rather than make assumptions.",
      "parentUuid": "d335383f_da63629f",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6579969_331561c0",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T20:20:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed with everything you said. Would there be some way to address my concern by flagging the value as bad then? Should we unset the value if we don\u0027t have a safe value to set it to?",
      "parentUuid": "b4168f17_ced97fa4",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ebbc6dd_8e59fd9d",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 1012457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T21:30:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unsetting the value seems a bit too drastic, I think, because this state may be transient and could auto-recover. For example, if the sequence ref is loose but temporarily not found due to NFS issues, we might fall back to the value from packed-refs, which would likely be outdated (non-incremental). However, the next time a read is attempted, it may return the latest value from the loose ref.\n\nWe are in a way flagging the value as bad by not allowing it to be used. However, I can\u0027t think of a good way to persist this behavior across service restarts.",
      "parentUuid": "b6579969_331561c0",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a274a60f_2ab299f1",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 442,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-29T21:36:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If jgit whould fall back to packed-refs, the update should fail on its own since it would still try to update the loose-ref. I think that if you have a sequence # that decrements, you want something drastic, you do not want any chance that the wrong value is used. Do you have a specific concern about unsetting the value? Are you concerned that it will be lost? If so, we could always set a \"bad\" value ref to save it so the admin at least knows what it was.",
      "parentUuid": "4ebbc6dd_8e59fd9d",
      "revId": "c90a46a5d8c6e1044cceb4bc96256735657bc2af",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
  ]
